1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
[narrator] Strange beasts and monsters.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
[squeaking]

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called...

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters.

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
[theme music playing]

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
[Hisoka Morow]
I've decided to let you live, for now.

14
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Until someday, you become
truly worthy of killing.

15
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,000
I will take it back.

16
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
But only when you can punch me
in the face like that.

17
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,000
In the meantime, you just hold onto it
for me.

18
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
TRAP x IN x THE HOLE

19
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[narrator]
Gon was utterly humiliated after Hisoka

20
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
returned the badges
that Geretta had taken.

21
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
As for Killua...

22
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
[Killua Zoldyck]
You're wasting your time.

23
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Follow me all you want, but
I'll never give you a chance to attack.

24
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
[Imori laughs]
Be afraid, kid.

25
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Be very afraid.

26
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
I'm a very cautious guy.

27
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
I'll do whatever it takes,

28
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
even when I'm up against a kid.

29
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Once he's exhausted,
then he has to go to sleep.

30
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
I'll strike.

31
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
[laughs]

32
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Like I said,
I'm a cautious guy.

33
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
[sighs]

34
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Come out or I'll come to you.

35
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:24,000
[Imori shudders]

36
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
This really is a pain, you know.

37
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Chances are,
you're only worth one lousy point.

38
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
[Imori]
He wants to fight?

39
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
He's just a kid.

40
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
I can't lose, right?

41
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,000
But...

42
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Why is he so relaxed?

43
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
He can't be that strong, can he?

44
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Right, be cautious.

45
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Because I'm a cautious guy.

46
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Oh, I should escape.
I mean, retreat and reassess.

47
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:00,000
But...

48
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
if I do, my brothers might yell at me.

49
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Wait, what am I saying?

50
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
If I go back without his badge,
they're definitely going to yell at me.

51
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
[whimpers]
Big brother!

52
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Huh?

53
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
We ran into a little trouble.

54
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
You must be done by now, right?

55
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
[all]
Huh?

56
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Uh....

57
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
-What are you, an idiot?
-[Imori yells]

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
You can't even beat a little kid?
Give me a break.

59
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Hold on, you've got it all wrong,
big brother.

60
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
What part do I have wrong?

61
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
I-- I didn't want to hurt
a little kid, that's all.

62
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
I thought I'd just hold off
and take it while he slept.

63
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
You're so full of it.

64
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
[Imori]
Fine, you got me.

65
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,000
And you're right.
I guess I should wrap this up.

66
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Time for a beat-down.

67
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
[Imori]
At least if I start to lose,

68
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
I've got my brothers here to step in
and back me up.

69
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
All right, kid.
How about you hand it over?

70
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Do as I say, and you won't get hurt.

71
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Idiot.

72
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,000
[grunts]

73
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
[Imori]
Don't go saying I didn't warn you.

74
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
[laughs]
Bam, right in the gut.

75
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
[Umori] It must hurt like hell.

76
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
-[Killua grunts]
-[Imori gasps]

77
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
What the hell, bro?
You go easy on this squirt?

78
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Yeah, you're way too nice, Imori.

79
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Oh... Uh, right.

80
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
You're number 198, huh?

81
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
[whimpers]
No way.

82
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,000
[gasps]

83
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Since it's only a number off
from the one I've been looking for,

84
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
I'm betting...

85
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,000
that 199 must be one of you two,
am I right?

86
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[Imori] Uh...

87
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Hey, Umori.

88
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Yeah.

89
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
-Get into formation. Let's do this.
-[gasps]

90
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
[Amori]
I'm pretty sure he ain't no ordinary kid.

91
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
[Imori panting]

92
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
[chuckles]

93
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
[grunts]

94
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
[Amori]
I don't give a damn how strong he is,

95
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
he doesn't stand a chance

96
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,000
against our group attack,
nobody does.

97
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
[Umori] The three of us have beaten
a lot tougher opponents than him

98
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,000
with this formation.

99
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
[Imori]
Just you wait, you brat.

100
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
We're gonna tear you to shreds.

101
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Uh... Up there.

102
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
[grunts]

103
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
-[gasps]
-Don't move, okay?

104
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,000
My fingers here cut a lot better
than any knife.

105
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:20,000
[Amori whimpers]

106
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[Killua sighs] Aw, man....
You're number 197.

107
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Damn, I really am bad
at guessing these things.

108
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
-Hey!
-Huh?

109
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Are you 199?

110
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Yeah.

111
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
[Killua]
Give it.

112
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
[grumbles]

113
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
-[grunts]
-Thank you.

114
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Now then,
for the ones I don't need.

115
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
[grumbles]

116
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Humph.

117
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,000
Oh...

118
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
And this one goes this way.

119
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
-[gasping]
-[Umori grunts]

120
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Good luck.
You've got three days left to find them.

121
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
I'll see you later.

122
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,000
[gasp]

123
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
[grunts] Damn.
[sighs]

124
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,000
[grunts]

125
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
Hm, number 197 was always with 199.

126
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
They were basically inseparable.

127
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:55,000
One thing's for sure, I never expected
that little kid to deal with him for me.

128
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
It's a good thing I was watching
from the shadows.

129
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Made it really easy to grab the badge
I nee-- [grunts]

130
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
[groans]

131
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
He... He knew.

132
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
The kid knew I was there!

133
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
[grumbles]

134
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
I failed.

135
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Oh man, this is so boring.

136
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
I wonder what Gon is up to right now.

137
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

138
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Hmm?

139
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,000
TOO BAD

140
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Humph!

141
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:48,000
[birds singing]

142
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[grunts]

143
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
We've been here for six days.

144
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Only one day left.

145
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
[Kurapika] It's been four days
since we ran into Hisoka.

146
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
And we haven't found anyone else.

147
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
[Leorio Paradinight] Hmm.

148
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Maybe we should
go back to the landing.

149
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
[Kurapika] Huh?

150
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[Leorio] It's possible there are
a few people who've already finished.

151
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
-[Kurapika] No, impossible.
-[Leorio] Huh?

152
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:29,000
This phase of the Exam is different
from all the others.

153
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
If your badge is stolen, you still have
the opportunity to recover it.

154
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
On the other hand,

155
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,000
just because you have six points worth
of badges now

156
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
doesn't guarantee you'll have them
when the phase ends.

157
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
This test can't be completed early.

158
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,000
I see.

159
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
[Kurapika]
But it's worth a shot.

160
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
With just a day left,

161
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,000
there must be a few
who've already gotten their six points.

162
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,000
And it's safe to assume they would
then gravitate to the same place.

163
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Near the goal.

164
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
At least, that's what I would do.

165
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Oh.

166
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
Okay, let's get going.

167
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
[Leorio]
Well? See anyone?

168
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
[Kurapika]
No.

169
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:33,000
That is to say,
no one who can be easily spotted.

170
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[Leorio]
Damn it.

171
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
[Kurapika] Perhaps we should split up
and keep looking.

172
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
But first, we should choose
a time and place for us to reconvene.

173
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
[Gon] And it will go way faster
with three people.

174
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[Kurapika and Leorio]
Huh?

175
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
[both]
Gon.

176
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,000
I guess we all must have had
exactly the same idea.

177
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
I've been watching from above

178
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
and it looks like there are
a lot of people nearby.

179
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Really? From above?

180
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Now why didn't we think of that?

181
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
It wouldn't have worked.

182
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Without eyes as sharp as Gon's,
we'd have never spotted anyone.

183
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,000
-[Kurapika] Gon.
-Huh?

184
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Were you able to get
all the badges you need?

185
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,000
[sighs]

186
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
[Gon]
Yeah, I guess.

187
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,000
-Oh, damn. You got yours, too?
-[Kurapika gasps]

188
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
So I'm the only one left.

189
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
[Gon]
Well, who's your target?

190
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
Number 246, a woman named Ponzu.

191
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:26,000
The only thing I really know about her
is that she uses chemical weapons.

192
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,000
[Leorio]
Gon.

193
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
You didn't happen to see any women
when you were up there, did you?

194
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
I'm afraid not.

195
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,000
I see.

196
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
All right. There are four possibilities
we should consider.

197
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:41,000
She's safe and still in possession
of her badge.

198
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:44,000
-She's alive but no longer has her badge.
-[crying]

199
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
She's out of the competition
but has held onto her badge.

200
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Or she's dead now,
and doesn't have her badge.

201
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[Leorio]
Do you really think

202
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,000
it's likely that she's both out
of the running and still has her badge?

203
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
She might have gotten
in some kind of accident.

204
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Or it's possible that she was defeated

205
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,000
after hiding her badge somewhere
for safe keeping.

206
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
If that's the case and she was killed
after concealing her badge,

207
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,000
her badge may never be found again.

208
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
The more you talk,
the worse this scenario gets.

209
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Hey, do you know anything else
about Ponzu?

210
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Like, does she wear some kind
of special fragrance, like Leorio?

211
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
-[Leorio] Huh?
-[Kurapika gasps] That's right.

212
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Gon might be able to track her
by her scent.

213
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Okay, but she might not even wear perfume,
you know, what do we do then?

214
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
-[Kurapika] He'll track her chemicals.
-Huh...

215
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:36,000
She's well known for using chemicals,
isn't she?

216
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:40,000
With a variety of chemicals,
some are sure to have distinct odors.

217
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
-Well, Gon?
-Right.

218
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
I'll give it a shot.

219
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
After all, it's why I'm here.

220
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Huh?

221
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
[Leorio]
Is she in there, Gon?

222
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
[Gon]
Yep, no doubt about it.

223
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
What's your plan?

224
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[Leorio]
I'm going in.

225
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,000
I want you guys to wait here.

226
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
[rattling echoes]

227
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[Leorio]
Doesn't look like there are any traps.

228
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
I'll head inside.

229
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Wait until I get the okay.

230
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Then you two can come in.

231
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,000
-[Kurapika] Thirty minutes.
-Hmm?

232
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
If after 30 minutes,
we haven't heard from you,

233
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
-we're coming to find you.
-Humph!

234
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,000
-[Leorio] No way.
-[both gasp]

235
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,000
If you don't hear from me,
you both go right back to the start.

236
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,000
-[Kurapika] That's not an option.
-Huh?

237
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
We have formed an alliance

238
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
and I will not abandon you now.

239
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,000
[sighs]

240
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Then this alliance is over.

241
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
I know it's selfish,
considering how much you helped me.

242
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
But I've got to do this alone.

243
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
-No way.
-[Leorio] Huh?

244
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,000
[yelling]
What did you say?

245
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
We're both staying here
because we want to.

246
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,000
[gasps]

247
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
It's our choice, so is that a problem?

248
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
[grumbles]

249
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
[sighs] Fine, suit yourself.

250
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,000
[gasps]

251
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Hang onto that for me.

252
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
[sigh]

253
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,000
[both chuckle]

254
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
[exhales]

255
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,000
[footsteps approaching]

256
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
[grunts, chuckles]

257
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
[Leorio]
I've just gotta go for it.

258
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,000
[footsteps echoing]

259
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,000
[breathes heavily]

260
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Hey isn't that... It's Bourbon.

261
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
-[woman] Let me guess.
-[gasps]

262
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:00,000
I must be your target, am I right?

263
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Ponzu!

264
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
-[Ponzu] It's pointless.
-Huh?

265
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
There's nothing for us to gain
by fighting down here.

266
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
I have everything to gain.

267
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
It's just like you said,

268
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:13,000
you're my target, all right!
This is happening, no matter what.

269
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,000
[sighs]

270
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Let's assume that we do fight and
by some miracle, you actually beat me.

271
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,000
There's still no way
you're ever getting out of this cave.

272
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Wait, what?

273
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
What are you talking about?

274
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:35,000
[chirping]

275
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
[Gon]
He's taking too long.

276
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
So what do you think,
is he okay?

277
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Yes.

278
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,000
But his 30 minutes are almost up.

279
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
[Leorio, shouting]
Kurapika, Gon!

280
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,000
-Don't come in!
-[both gasp]

281
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
[Gon]
Leorio!

282
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,000
[gasp]

283
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
[grunts]

284
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Huh?

285
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
[Gon]
Leorio!

286
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
You idiots.

287
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
I thought I told you
not to come in.

288
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
[Kurapika]
He's covered in bites.

289
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,000
If those snakes are venomous, then...

290
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
They're a kind of viper.

291
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,000
And they are poisonous,
but it isn't that strong.

292
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
Still, with this many bites...

293
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
[Leorio groaning]
Stop it, will you?

294
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:47,000
One cut in your mouth,
or even a little cavity...

295
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Don't worry about it.

296
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:52,000
[Kurapika] Leorio,
do you have any anti-venom in here?

297
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,000
If I did...

298
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,000
maybe...

299
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
I would have been able...

300
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
to save you guys, at least.

301
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,000
[sighs]

302
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Leorio!

303
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Let's stop the bleeding.

304
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
[breathing heavily]

305
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:12,000
That should do it.

306
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,000
We still need to get him to a doctor.

307
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
-[Ponzu] I wouldn't advise that.
-[Gon and Kurapika gasp]

308
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
You aren't getting out so easily.

309
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,000
What do you mean by that?

310
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,000
[Ponzu]
What I mean is that we're trapped.

311
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Whenever someone tries
to leave this cave...

312
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
[hissing]

313
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,000
...the snakes will attack you en masse.

314
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,000
[gasp]

315
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
[loud hissing]

316
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
It's a trap set by Bourbon,
the snake charmer.

317
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
If you're bitten,

318
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:50,000
you'll end up completely paralyzed,
just like your friend here.

319
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,000
After that, you die.

320
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
[Kurapika] Bourbon, you're looking
to collect more badges, right?

321
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
We'll give you every one we have.

322
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
Just please, let us out of here.

323
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Don't bother.

324
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
[Ponzu]
You see, he's already dead.

325
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
[Kurapika]
What? You can't be serious.

326
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:34,000
[narrator] Gon and friends
are caught in a trap set by Bourbon,

327
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
the snake charmer,
and can't leave the cave.

328
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,000
Will they pass the Hunter Exam?

329
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:45,000
And will Leorio survive
the venomous snake bites?

330
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,000
[hissing]

331
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,000
[grunts]

332
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:01,000
[theme song playing]

333
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Gon] Next time,
"Big x Time x Interview."

334
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Thanks a lot, Kurapika.

335
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
[Kurapika]
No, thank you, Gon.
